        rules: {
          objective: 'Score 60 points through winning tricks and declarations.',
          gameplay: "Standard trick taking. Must follow suit. If you can't follow, you MUST trump. Higher card of the led suit or higher trump wins the trick.",
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit when possible; if void in led suit, must trump.',
            'Higher card of led suit wins unless trumped; higher trump wins the trick.',
            'Score 60 points through tricks and declarations (marriage) to win.',
            'Last trick awards 10 bonus points.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Keep track of the Aces. In a 32-card deck, Aces are nearly impossible to beat unless someone trumps. If you have the lead, play your Aces early to secure point-tricks before the opponent can void a suit.',
          intermediate: "Trump Management: Use the exchange (if allowed in your variant) to build a 'Long Suit'. If you can control the trump suit with 4-5 cards, you can dominate the end-game and capture the opponent's high-value side cards.",
          advanced: "The 'Seven Swap': If you have the 7 of trumps, don't swap it too early. Wait until the opponent leads a high trump, then swap and play the new trump to seize the lead. This defensive move can break their momentum.",
          tips: [
            'Memory: Since 12 cards are dealt to each, and 8 are in the talon, you initially know 12/32 cards. Pay attention to the trump card!',
            "Focus on the 'Last Trick' (10 bonus points) as it often determines the winner in a close 60-point match.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
